Checked again in headless Chrome, at 1440x900, 1280x800 and 390x844, on a
board built from the branch's new head with all of the above stored. The check
read every text node outside scripts, styles and textareas, every attribute of
every element, every input's value and the tab title, on `/`, `/config` (loaded
and reached by the header link), `/tasks/new`, a task's page, and "Task not
found" (loaded and reached by a link). It found an override, embedding or
isolate only in three `data-` attributes on the board page
(`data-project-name`, `data-title-suffix`, `data-status-label`). Those hold the
stored text for the script to read; nothing draws them as they are. Textareas
were skipped because they are the editors that keep stored text by design.

The tests are `TestHandlerClientDrawsAttachmentNamesWithoutDirectionOverrides`,
`TestHandlerPageDrawsTypedTextWithoutDirectionOverrides`,
